<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<workflow>
  <name>job_data_vault_all_incl_md</name>
  <name_sync_with_filename>Y</name_sync_with_filename>
  <description>Complete run to load the Data Vault</description>
  <extended_description>This job first refreshes the metadata for a Data vault and then loads it completely
(or only partially depending on the 'process_' parameters), based on the value of parameter id_data_vault.
The steps are:

 1:	Refresh Data Vault metadata
 2:	Create necessary hub-run tables
 3:	Load all hubs
 4:	Create necessary link-run tables
 5:	Load all links
 6:	Load all 'regular' link validity satellites (lnk_bk_columns filled).
 7:	Load all 'group' link validity satellites (lnk_group_key_column filled).
 8:	Load all hub satellites
 9:	Load all hub status satellites  (to identify deletes, needs FULL load!)
10:	Load all link satellites
11:	Load all link status satellites (to identify deletes, needs FULL load!)

The 'process_'-parameters define which steps will be processed.
The default for all of them is 1 (process), but if a run crashed while processing the link satellites you might want to
restart at that point instead of processing all objects again.

If the run is a restart (parameter ind_restart = 1) the load_dts of the previous job is used as the load_dts for the run.
That will ensure consistent start/end dates in the satellites.
That previous run should not be succesfully finished, except when parameter ind_force_restart = 1.
</extended_description>
  <workflow_version>1.12</workflow_version>
  <workflow_status>0</workflow_status>
